  "description": "WHBB Nut Cup, 1 November 2026, on BB_Nut's Discord: a slightly modified NAFC ruleset, 3 games, Swiss pairing. Every team picks ONE package for its tier: 1,150,000 gold plus the tier's skills, OR 1,100,000 gold plus one extra PRIMARY skill. Unspent gold is lost. Tiers (skills = total added skills; a secondary slot may always hold a primary): T1 Amazon, Orc, Old World Alliance - 4 skills, no secondary. T2 Dark Elf, Nurgle, Underworld Denizens, Wood Elf - 5 skills, no secondary. T3 Elven Union, Human, Lizardmen, Necromantic Horror, Norse, Skaven, Shambling Undead - 6 skills, up to 1 secondary. T4 Black Orc, Chaos Chosen, Chaos Dwarf, Chaos Renegade, Dwarf, Imperial Nobility, Khorne, Vampire - 7 skills, up to 1 secondary. T5 Goblin, Halfling - 8 skills, up to 2 secondary OR 1 Star Player (a team that hires a star gets no secondary slots). Skills are free of gold and all assigned before the event; ONE player may take two skills (at most one secondary, and only where the tier allows secondaries), every other player at most one; skills may be duplicated across players; no stat increases, no random skills. Inducements: Bribes 0-3, Blitzer's Best Kegs 0-2, Halfling Master Chef 0-1 (Halfling only), Mortuary Assistant 0-1, Plague Doctor 0-1, Riotous Rookies 0-1, Team Mascot 0-1, Weather Mage 0-1; Star Player 0-1 (Tier 5 only). Stars (Tier 5): max one, no extra skills; paired stars (Grak & Crumbleberry, Dribl & Drull, Lucien & Valen Swift) count as two and are not selectable; banned: Bomber Dribblesnot, Cindy Piewhistle, Hakflem Skuttlespike, Morg 'n' Thorg, Skitter Stab-Stab. Everything else NAFC / BB2025 default; minimum 11 players.",
  "dataNote": "Transcribed from the organiser's Google Doc. Machine-enforced: tiers, the two packages per tier (Tier 5 also carries two Star packages with 0 secondary, which is how 'a star replaces the secondaries' is encoded), skill counts, one stacked player, inducement list/caps incl. Halfling-only Chef, star bans and the one-star cap. Hand-check: 'no random skills' (the builder only offers chosen skills, but a submitted sheet cannot show how a skill was picked); Bribes are capped at 3 even for Bribery and Corruption teams (the doc lists Bribes 0-3 for all tiers).",
